{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":18408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"04206ae7f73e0a7a403a0ad0b24712c8","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I have the Photo_Profile image (a silhouette walking into light). Now let me build the design.\n\nPlan:\n- Page 03 · Workspace (4:2), empty.\n- Create components: Header (variant Work/About current), Footer, NavLink, ProjectBlock, SkillList, ContactBlock, ImagePlaceholder.\n- Create two frames: 01_Work and 02_About, 1440 wide, light mode.\n- Colors: ink #181717, accent #2429AF, background light (e.g., #FAFAF7 or white), secondary gray.\n- DM Sans font.\n- Wire prototype: nav About → 02_About, logo \"da.\" → 01_Work, Work nav → 01_Work.\n\nCopy:\nWork page:\n- Header: logo \"da.\", nav Work/About/Playground/Contact, current: Work\n- Intro: \"Hello, I'm Deniz.\" + \"A senior-year design student who is trying to specialize in 3D modeling & texturing.\" + scroll cue (Icon_Arrow_Down)\n- Projects:\n  1. 01 / Goblin Bust — \"Goblin concept digital sculpture with human-like skin. Learned a lot of quick tips and look development.\" tools: \"Sculpted in ZBrush, retopologized and UV-mapped in Maya, textured in Mari, rendered with Arnold.\" link \"More shots from this project ↗\"\n  2. 02 / Skin Shader Study — \"Subsurface weight, specular roughness and diffuse maps generated with procedural and manual techniques.\" link \"See case study →\"\n  3. 03 / Creature Concept — \"Experimental creature modeling for a school project.\" status \"Project WIP\"\n- Footer: \"Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020\" · Artstation · LinkedIn · Twitter\n\nAbout page:\n- Header current: About\n- Intro: \"Hi, I'm Deniz Arslan, 3D artist & sculptor.\" + biography 2 paragraphs + Photo_Profile\n- Skills: Main Software list, Main Skills list\n- Contact: \"I'd be thrilled to hear about your next project\" (Icon_Arrow_Right) · \"deniz.arslan@example.com\" · \"View Resume\"\n- Footer\n\nNote: the \"⏤\" character is U+2E4F (double dash em dash horizontal bar). Use it as given in \"Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020\" and \"Istanbul ⏤ currently\".\n\nLet me write the build code in manageable steps:\n\nStep 1: Load fonts, set up page, create components (NavLink, Header, Footer, Placeholder, ProjectBlock, SkillList, ContactBlock).\nStep 2: Build 01_Work frame.\nStep 3: Build 02_About frame.\nStep 4: Wire prototype reactions.\nStep 5: Screenshots and verify.\n\nFont families: DM Sans - need Regular, Medium, Bold, maybe Italic. Let me load \"DM Sans\" with Regular, Medium, Bold.\n\nDesign system:\n- bg: #F7F6F2 (warm off-white) or #FAFAFA. Let me use #F5F4F0 subtle warm light.\n- text primary: #181717\n- text secondary: #6B6A66 (warm gray)\n- divider: #E3E1DB\n- accent: #2429AF\n- placeholder bg: #E8E6E0 with ink 20% text\n\nLayout: 1440 wide, content margin 96px each side (content width 1248). Header fixed at top: logo left, nav right, 88px tall. Footer: left \"Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020\", right links.\n\nWork page:\n- Header\n- Intro section: big heading \"Hello, I'm Deniz.\" (96px bold), sub \"A senior-year design student who is trying to specialize in 3D modeling & texturing.\" (24px, secondary), scroll cue Icon_Arrow_Down below with \"Scroll\" label maybe.\n- Projects: three rows. Each: number \"01\", name \"Goblin Bust\" (large), description, tools line, link, and image placeholder (right side). Alternate? Keep consistent: image right, text left. Or image left alternating. Keep consistent for cleanliness.\n- Footer.\n\nAbout page:\n- Header (current About)\n- Intro: heading \"Hi, I'm Deniz Arslan, 3D artist & sculptor.\" + photo + bio paragraphs\n- Skills: two columns \"Main Software\" and \"Main Skills\"\n- Contact block: big \"I'd be thrilled to hear about your next project\" with arrow icon, email link \"deniz.arslan@example.com\", \"View Resume\" link.\n- Footer.\n\nComponents to create (reusable):\n- NavLink (text, state current/regular)\n- Header (component, used in both pages with instance swap for current state — I'll make header as component with variants? Simpler: create a \"Header\" component with variant property Current: Work/About.) Variants via component properties: create two headers and combine as variants. That might be complex via API but doable. Alternatively create single Header component where nav items are instances of NavLink component; then for About page use an instance of Header and override? Current state differences can't be instance-swapped on text easily. Simplest: Header component with variants \"Current=Work\" and \"Current=About\". I'll build that.\n\nActually to keep it manageable: build Header as a component set with two variants. Build Footer component. Build ProjectBlock component. Build SkillGroup component. Build ImagePlaceholder component. NavLink as component with variants (Default/Current).\n\nLet me write code. I need to be careful with Figma plugin API:\n- figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"DM Sans\", style:\"Regular\"}) etc. DM Sans styles: \"Regular\", \"Medium\", \"Bold\". Actually DM Sans has \"Regular\", \"Italic\", \"Medium\", \"Medium Italic\", \"Bold\", \"Bold Italic\". Use Regular, Medium, Bold.\n\n- Instances of components on other pages: component is on page 1:4 (media page). To create an instance on workspace page: const inst = comp.createInstance(); then workspace.appendChild(inst) or frame.appendChild(inst). createInstance places it on current page, so set current page to workspace first: await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(workspacePage). Then createInstance works and lands on that page.\n\nIcon recolor: instance children fills. I'll set fills on the vector inside instance by findAll.\n\nFor arrow links: \"More shots from this project ↗\" — the ↗ is a text char, fine. \"See case study →\" text char fine. The must-include for Contact says (Icon_Arrow_Right) — so include the icon component next to the contact headline. Scroll cue uses Icon_Arrow_Down.\n\nNow write build code. I'll do it in a few calls.\n\nCall 1: setup — load fonts, find page 4:2, set current page, define colors/helpers, create NavLink component variants, Header component set, Footer component.\n\nActually creating components with variants programmatically: create component nodes, then figma.combineAsVariants([a,b], parent). Then instances: inst = componentSet.defaultVariant.createInstance() — for ComponentSetNode, use componentSet.createInstance()? In plugin API, ComponentSetNode has createInstance(). Then set variant via inst.setProperties({\"Current\": \"About\"}).\n\nSimplify: Instead of variants, I can make Header a single component designed for Work page, then for About page... no, better to do variants properly. Or, simpler approach: make \"Nav\" items components with a boolean \"current\" — can't per instance without variants.\n\nI'll go with component sets for Header (Current: Work | About) and NavLink not needed separately then — header variants embed everything. Footer single component. ProjectBlock single component (content overridden via instance text overrides — allowed: text overrides in instances). But cleaner to just build project blocks as frames with component instances of shared pieces. The brief says \"Design the header, footer, link style, current-page state and every content block as reusable components\". So ProjectBlock as component with text overridden per instance is fine. SkillList component. ContactBlock component. ImagePlaceholder component.\n\nText overrides in instances: find text nodes inside instance and set characters. That works.\n\nLet me structure:\n\nComponents (create on workspace page in a components area at the side, e.g., x=4000):\n1. Header (component set, variants Current=Work, Current=About)\n2. Footer\n3. ProjectBlock\n4. SkillGroup\n5. ContactBlock\n6. ImagePlaceholder\n7. Link/TextLink maybe overkill — link style = accent color + underline on hover; just style consistently.\n\nBuild frames:\n- 01_Work: frame x=0, y=0, w=1440, h≈2200 auto.\n- 02_About: x=1640, y=0, w=1440.\n\nHeader layout: 1440 wide, height 96, padding-x 96. Logo \"da.\" left (28px Bold, ink). Nav right: Work, About, Playground, Contact (16px Medium; current = ink + accent underline bar or accent dot; non-current = gray #6B6A66). Bottom divider line.\n\nFooter: height 120, top divider, left text \"Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020\" (14px gray), right: Artstation LinkedIn Twitter (14px medium ink, links).\n\nIntro (Work): padding 96. Top spacing after header ~120. Label small \"PORTFOLIO ⏤ 3D ART\" maybe not needed. Heading \"Hello, I'm Deniz.\" 96px Bold ink. Sub 24px Regular secondary, max width 640. Then scroll cue: Icon_Arrow_Down instance + text \"Scroll to explore\" 13px caps gray. Maybe a big layout with heading left and meta right.\n\nProjects section: title \"Selected Work\" small caps. Each project row: \n- left column (number \"01\" accent 16px bold, name 40px bold ink, description 16px regular secondary max 480, tools 14px regular gray italic? keep regular, link \"More shots from this project ↗\" accent 16px medium)\n- right: ImagePlaceholder 640×420.\nDivider between projects.\n\nProject 3 status \"Project WIP\": a pill/badge with dot, gray, not a link.\n\nPlaceholder: rect fill #E9E7E1, dashed stroke? Figma strokes can be dashed via dashPattern. Plus diagonal? Keep: fill #ECEAE4, 1px stroke #D8D5CD, centered icon/text \"Project image ⏤ placeholder\" 14px gray. \n\nAbout page:\n- Header Current=About\n- Intro section: heading \"Hi, I'm Deniz Arslan, 3D artist & sculptor.\" 64px bold. Layout: text left (width ~720), photo right (Photo_Profile instance, crop 360×480). Bio paragraphs under heading.\n- Skills: two SkillGroup components side by side with divider.\n- Contact block: big text \"I'd be thrilled to hear about your next project\" with Icon_Arrow_Right, email link large, \"View Resume\" link. \n- Footer.\n\nContactBlock: heading row with icon arrow right 32px? Icon is 24. Scale instance to 32. Text \"I'd be thrilled to hear about your next project\" 48px bold. Below: email \"deniz.arslan@example.com\" accent link 20px, and \"View Resume ↗\"? Brief says \"View Resume\" plain text link. Keep \"View Resume\".\n\nPrototype wiring:\n- In Header (Work variant): About nav text → 02_About (on click navigate). Logo \"da.\" → 01_Work. Work nav → 01_Work (self).\n- In Header (About variant): logo → 01_Work, Work nav → 01_Work.\nReactions must be set on nodes inside the component so they propagate to instances. Reactions on component internals work: set node.reactions inside the main component.\n\nLet me also give the whole top-level frames vertical scroll? Not needed.\n\nNow write the code. Careful with:\n- figma.setCurrentPageAsync required.\n- load fonts before creating text: DM Sans Regular/Medium/Bold.\n- combineAsVariants needs parent.\n- For icon instances inside other pages: create instance then resize (instances can resize). Recolor: instance.findAll(n=>n.type===\"VECTOR\") set fills.\n\nLet me now write call 1: setup + tokens + NavLink-ish + Header + Footer components.\n\nI'll write helpers inline each call (state isn't persisted between calls? Actually each use_figma call runs a fresh script — variables don't persist. So include helpers each time. Also need to fetch nodes by ID from previous calls — return IDs and reuse).\n\nLet me carefully write the code.\n\nCall 1:\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"4:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nawait Promise.all([\n  figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"DM Sans\", style:\"Regular\"}),\n  figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"DM Sans\", style:\"Medium\"}),\n  figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"DM Sans\", style:\"Bold\"}),\n]);\nconst INK = {r:0.094,g:0.090,b:0.090};       // #181717\nconst ACCENT = {r:0.141,g:0.161,b:0.686};    // #2429AF\nconst BG = {r:0.973,g:0.969,b:0.957};        // #F8F7F4\nconst GRAY = {r:0.42,g:0.41,b:0.39};         // #6B6863\nconst LINE = {r:0.878,g:0.871,b:0.847};      // #E0DED8\nconst PLACEHOLDER = {r:0.925,g:0.918,b:0.894}; // #ECEAE4\nfunction txt(chars, size, style, color){ const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:\"DM Sans\",style}; t.characters=chars; t.fontSize=size; t.fills=[{type:\"SOLID\",color}]; return t; }\n...\n```\n\nHeader construction: I'll build a function buildHeader(current) returning a component node.\n\nHeader 1440×96: \n- layoutMode HORIZONTAL? Simpler absolute positioning inside component. Use auto layout: component.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\", width 1440 fixed, padding left/right 96, height 96, itemSpacing auto with counter axis alignment center. Logo left, nav group right. Auto layout with space-between: set primaryAxisAlignItems=\"SPACE_BETWEEN\" after adding logo + nav frame.\n\nNav frame: auto layout horizontal, itemSpacing 40, children: 4 text nodes. Current item: ink color + Medium + small underline accent bar (2px height rect under text, accent). Non-current: gray.\n\nTo make underline: wrap nav item in vertical auto layout with text + 2px bar (bar visible only current; for others make bar transparent or omit). For simplicity, build nav item as a frame with text and an accent bar rect; hide bar for non-current (visible=false). \n\nFooter component: 1440×120 auto layout horizontal space-between padding 96, top border: add a 1px line rect at top inside? Easier: footer frame with stroke top only — strokes apply all around. Use a line: figma.createLine? createLine exists (LineNode). Line width 1308 at x=96,y=0. In auto layout that complicates. Alternative: put divider as separate rectangle child with absolute positioning inside footer (component not auto-layout). Let me do footer as absolute-position component: rect line (1308×1, fill LINE) at top, left text, right links group.\n\nActually simplest robust: make footer a fixed-size frame (1440×120) with layoutMode NONE and place children absolutely:\n- line: rect x=96 y=0 w=1308 h=1 fill LINE\n- left text at x=96, y=64\n- right links: auto layout frame at right? Position frame x computed. Right group: auto layout with three texts itemSpacing 32; place at x = 1440-96-groupWidth, y=58. To know width, after creating, group.x = 1440-96-group.width.\n\nFine.\n\nProjectBlock component: fixed 1308 wide? Make it part of frame layout. ProjectBlock: auto layout horizontal, itemSpacing 64, width 1308, padding? Left text column (auto layout vertical, spacing 20): number+name row, description (fixed width 560), tools (fixed width 560, optional), link/status. Right: ImagePlaceholder 620×420.\n\nTo handle variants (project 2 has no tools), instances: I can override by deleting/hiding nodes in instance? Hiding instance children is allowed (visible=false). Yes — instance children can be hidden. So tools text hidden for project 2, link text changed, status pill vs link: for project 3 hide link, show status. So include both link and status pill in component; default: link visible, status hidden. Instance 3: hide link, show status. Instance 2: hide tools.\n\nImagePlaceholder component: 620×420 rect fill PLACEHOLDER, stroke dashed LINE-darker, centered label \"Project image — placeholder\" 14px gray. Dash: rect.dashPattern=[8,6]; strokes.\n\nSkillGroup component: vertical auto layout: title \"Main Software\" small caps 13px medium gray letter-spacing, divider, then list of items text 18px regular ink, each row with small dot? Items separated by dividers? Keep simple: items as text lines 18px with 14 spacing, itemSpacing 16. Instance overrides: title and items — items as a single text with line breaks (each item on new line, lineHeight). Single text node easier to override.\n\nSkillGroup: title text + body text (multi-line with \\n). Body 20px Regular ink, lineHeight 36. Maybe with a 1px divider between title and body.\n\nContactBlock: vertical: row [headline 48 bold ink, Icon_Arrow_Right instance 32 accent], divider? then email link 20 medium accent, \"View Resume\" 20 medium ink with underline? Links: accent color for email; \"View Resume\" accent too? Make links accent with underline decoration. Keep consistent: all text links = accent #2429AF, medium, with underline on hover (can't do hover easily; skip). Actually project links earlier were planned accent. Nav links gray/ink. Consistent link style: accent + Medium. Underline optional; I'll underline the email maybe not. Keep accent, no underline, medium.\n\nIcon_Arrow_Right next to contact headline: instance scaled 40, recolored accent.\n\nNow the scroll cue in Work intro: Icon_Arrow_Down 28 accent or ink + \"Scroll\" label.\n\nPrototype: after frames built, set reactions:\n- Work frame: header instance (variant Work) — reactions must be set on the component's inner nodes (in main component), which propagate to instances. But navigation targets differ per instance? No — targets are same frames: logo→01_Work, About→02_About, Work→01_Work. Same for both variants. So set reactions inside the component variants' inner nodes. \n\nReactions on inner nodes of a main component: instances inherit them. Yes, that works in Figma prototypes.\n\nAlso the brief links: on 01_Work, \"→ About (nav) → 02_About → logo 'da.', Work (nav) → 01_Work (self)\". On 02_About: \"→ logo 'da.', Work (nav) → 01_Work\". So About nav link in About header has no required reaction (it's self/current) — fine.\n\nSet reactions: node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, action:{type:\"NODE\", destinationId:\"<frameId>\", navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:null }}]. In new API: actions use {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\"...} or null, ...}. I'll use simple: action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:id,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:null,presetDuration:0.3? } Not needed. Let me just use transition null. Some API versions require \"preserveScrollPosition\":false. Include it.\n\nNote: reactions on text nodes inside auto layout — fine.\n\nAlso add flow starting points? Prototype flows get created automatically when reactions exist; add a flow starting point on 01_Work: figma.currentPage.flowStartingPoints = [{nodeId: workFrameId, name:\"Work\"}]? flowStartingPoints is a page property (readonly? it's writable via page.flowStartingPoints = [...]). I think it's writable. I'll try; wrap in try/catch.\n\nAlso media component icons: getNodeByIdAsync(\"2:2\") etc., then createInstance inside frames — instance of component from another page in same file is fine.\n\nPhoto_Profile instance: resize to 384×512? Original 228×320 ratio 0.7125. For about page: 408×572 maybe too tall. Use 384×539? Let me do 400×561. Hmm, layout: about intro: heading+bio left (width 700), photo right 440×616. That's tall; total frame height maybe ~2100. Fine.\n\nActually simpler: photo 420×588 (ratio 0.714 ≈ 228/320=0.7125 ✓). 420/0.7125=589.5. Use 424×595.\n\nLet me be careful with auto layout + absolute mixes. I'll mostly use auto layout for frames with fixed widths on text via textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\" and fixed width via resize.\n\nPlan top-level frame structure:\n- 01_Work: vertical auto layout, fill BG, width 1440, itemSpacing 0, padding 0, primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO (hug height), counter fixed 1440.\n  - header instance (1440)\n  - intro section (auto layout vertical, padding 96 top 160 bottom 120, spacing 48)\n  - projects section (padding 96, spacing 120, vertical)\n  - footer instance\n- 02_About: similar.\n\nFor text widths: set layoutAlign \"STRETCH\"? For text inside auto-layout vertical frame: t.layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\" makes width fill; with textAutoResize HEIGHT. Good for paragraphs.\n\nLet me write the code now. Multiple calls:\n\nCall A: setup, tokens, helper funcs defined, create ImagePlaceholder component, Footer component, Header component set (two variants). Return IDs.\n\nCall B: create ProjectBlock, SkillGroup, ContactBlock components. Return IDs.\n\nCall C: build 01_Work frame with instances + content overrides.\n\nCall D: build 02_About frame.\n\nCall E: prototype reactions + flow start + verify (query nodes).\n\nCall F: screenshots of both frames; fix issues.\n\nHelper functions must be redefined in each call. Fonts loaded once per call (each call needs loadFontAsync before setting characters — fonts stay loaded in the doc session? Safer to load in each call before text ops).\n\nWatch out: DM Sans \"Medium\" style exists? DM Sans styles: Regular, Italic, Medium, Medium Italic, Bold, Bold Italic. Yes Medium exists.\n\nIcon recolor: icons neutral #1A1A1F — recolor to fit system. For arrow down (scroll cue): ink or gray. For arrow right (contact): accent.\n\nInstance resize: instances can be resized if the component supports constraints — just call resize on instance, allowed.\n\nOne caution: creating instances of components located on other pages — createInstance() adds to current page root by default? Actually it appends to figma.currentPage. We set current page to workspace. Then we appendChild into target frame.\n\nFor component override text: const t = inst.findOne(n => n.name === \"...\" && n.type===\"TEXT\"); then set t.characters (need font loaded).\n\nAlright. Also name frames exactly \"01_Work\" and \"02_About\".\n\nAlso, components area: place components at x=3200+ on workspace page so they don't overlap frames. Or place on workspace page directly (not in a frame) — top-level components on the page are fine. The brief wants components \"in your file\" — top-level on workspace page is fine, but to keep tidy, group them in a section? Sections are nice: figma.createSection? Sections can't contain component sets? They can. I'll place components in a row at y offset far right (x=2000..), frames at x=0 and x=1600. Actually put frames first: 01_Work at x=0, 02_About at x=1600, components row at x=0, y=2600 (below). Simpler: components below frames at y=2800.\n\nHmm — but frames' heights ~2200-2500. Place components at y=3000.\n\nLet me write Call A now.\n\nDetailed code Call A:\n\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"4:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nconst fonts = [\n  {family:\"DM Sans\", style:\"Regular\"},\n  {family:\"DM Sans\", style:\"Medium\"},\n  {family:\"DM Sans\", style:\"Bold\"},\n];\nfor (const f of fonts) await figma.loadFontAsync(f);\n\nconst C = {\n  ink:{r:24/255,g:23/255,b:23/255},\n  accent:{r:36/255,g:41/255,b:175/255},\n  bg:{r:248/255,g:247/255,b:244/255},\n  gray:{r:107/255,g:104/255,b:99/255},\n  line:{r:224/255,g:222/255,b:216/255},\n  ph:{r:236/255,g:234/255,b:228/255},\n  white:{r:1,g:1,b:1},\n};\nfunction solid(c){return [{type:\"SOLID\",color:c}];}\nfunction text(chars,{size=16,style=\"Regular\",color=C.ink,caps=false,ls,align,lh}={}){\n  const t=figma.createText();\n  t.fontName={family:\"DM Sans\",style};\n  t.characters=chars;\n  t.fontSize=size;\n  t.fills=solid(color);\n  if(caps)t.textCase=\"UPPER\";\n  if(ls!==undefined)t.letterSpacing={unit:\"PIXELS\",value:ls};\n  if(lh!==undefined)t.lineHeight={unit:\"PIXELS\",value:lh};\n  if(align)t.textAlignHorizontal=align;\n  return t;\n}\nfunction hline(w,color=C.line){const r=figma.createRectangle();r.resize(w,1);r.fills=solid(color);return r;}\n```\n\nImagePlaceholder component:\n```js\nconst ph = figma.createComponent();\nph.name=\"ImagePlaceholder\";\nph.resize(620,420);\nph.fills=solid(C.ph);\nph.strokes=[{type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:200/255,g:198/255,b:192/255}}];\nph.strokeWeight=1; ph.dashPattern=[10,8]; ph.strokeAlign=\"INSIDE\";\nph.cornerRadius=8;\nph.layoutMode=\"VERTICAL\";\nph.primaryAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\"; ph.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";\nph.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\"; ph.counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";\nph.itemSpacing=10;\nconst phLabel=text(\"PROJECT IMAGE — PLACEHOLDER\",{size:13,style:\"Medium\",color:C.gray,ls:1.5});\nph.appendChild(phLabel);\npage.appendChild(ph); ph.x=0; ph.y=3000;\n```\nWait dashPattern on RectangleNode: property is dashPattern — yes exists on GeometryMixin.\n\nFooter component:\n```js\nconst footer=figma.createComponent();\nfooter.name=\"Footer\";\nfooter.resize(1440,140);\nfooter.fills=solid(C.bg);\nconst fl=hline(1308); fl.x=96; fl.y=0; footer.appendChild(fl);\nconst fLeft=text(\"Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020\",{size:15,style:\"Medium\",color:C.gray});\nfLeft.x=96; fLeft.y=80; footer.appendChild(fLeft);\nconst fRight=figma.createFrame(); fRight.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\"; fRight.itemSpacing=36; fRight.fills=[];\nfor(const s of [\"Artstation\",\"LinkedIn\",\"Twitter\"]){const l=text(s,{size:15,style:\"Medium\",color:C.ink}); fRight.appendChild(l);}\nfooter.appendChild(fRight);\nfRight.x=1440-96-fRight.width; fRight.y=78;\nfooter.clipsContent=false;\npage.appendChild(footer); footer.x=0; footer.y=3520;\n```\n\nAuto layout frame default sizing: primaryAxisSizingMode default FIXED? New frames default layoutMode NONE. When setting layoutMode, default sizing mode is FIXED both axes? In plugin API, when you set layoutMode, sizing modes default to \"AUTO\"? Actually default primaryAxisSizingMode is \"AUTO\" and counterAxisSizingMode \"AUTO\" I believe when created via createFrame then set layoutMode... Hmm not guaranteed. Safer: after appending children, fRight has hug behavior if sizing AUTO. If FIXED with default 100×100, children overflow. I'll explicitly set both sizing modes to \"AUTO\" for hug frames.\n\nHeader variants:\n```js\nfunction navItem(label,current){\n  const f=figma.createFrame(); f.layoutMode=\"VERTICAL\"; f.itemSpacing=8; f.fills=[];\n  f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"; f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";\n  f.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";\n  const t=text(label,{size:15,style:current?\"Bold\":\"Medium\",color:current?C.ink:C.gray});\n  f.appendChild(t);\n  const bar=figma.createRectangle(); bar.resize(t.width,2); bar.fills=solid(C.accent); bar.cornerRadius=1;\n  bar.visible=current;\n  f.appendChild(bar);\n  return f;\n}\nfunction buildHeader(current){\n  const h=figma.createComponent(); h.name=\"Current=\"+current;\n  h.resize(1440,96); h.fills=solid(C.bg);\n  const logo=text(\"da.\",{size:26,style:\"Bold\",color:C.ink}); logo.name=\"Logo\";\n  logo.x=96; logo.y=(96-logo.height)/2; h.appendChild(logo);\n  const nav=figma.createFrame(); nav.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\"; nav.itemSpacing=44; nav.fills=[];\n  nav.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"; nav.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";\n  for(const s of [\"Work\",\"About\",\"Playground\",\"Contact\"]){const it=navItem(s,s===current); it.name=\"Nav_\"+s; nav.appendChild(it);}\n  h.appendChild(nav);\n  nav.x=1440-96-nav.width; nav.y=(96-nav.height)/2;\n  const ln=hline(1308); ln.x=96; ln.y=95; h.appendChild(ln);\n  return h;\n}\nconst hWork=buildHeader(\"Work\");\nconst hAbout=buildHeader(\"About\");\n// place near each other then combine\nhWork.x=0; hWork.y=3160; hAbout.x=0; hAbout.y=3300;\npage.appendChild(hWork); page.appendChild(hAbout);\nconst headerSet=figma.combineAsVariants([hWork,hAbout],page);\nheaderSet.name=\"Header\"; headerSet.x=0; headerSet.y=3160;\n```\n\ncombineAsVariants wraps in a component set; positions might shift — fine.\n\nReturn IDs: headerSet, footer, ph.\n\nCall B: ProjectBlock, SkillGroup, ContactBlock.\n\nProjectBlock (component, default content = project 1):\n```js\nconst pb=figma.createComponent(); pb.name=\"ProjectBlock\";\npb.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\"; pb.itemSpacing=72; pb.fills=[];\npb.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"; pb.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";\nconst col=figma.createFrame(); col.layoutMode=\"VERTICAL\"; col.itemSpacing=0; col.fills=[];\ncol.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"; col.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";\n// number + title\nconst head=figma.createFrame(); head.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\"; head.itemSpacing=20; head.fills=[];\nhead.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"; head.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"; head.counterAxisAlignItems=\"BASELINE\"? \n```\ncounterAxisAlignItems accepts \"MIN\",\"CENTER\",\"MAX\",\"BASELINE\". Yes BASELINE allowed.\n\n```js\nconst num=text(\"01\",{size:16,style:\"Bold\",color:C.accent}); num.name=\"Number\";\nconst title=text(\"Goblin Bust\",{size:36,style:\"Bold\",color:C.ink}); title.name=\"Title\";\nhead.appendChild(num); head.appendChild(title);\ncol.appendChild(head);\nconst desc=text(\"Goblin concept digital sculpture with human-like skin. Learned a lot of quick tips and look development.\",{size:17,style:\"Regular\",color:C.gray,lh:28});\ndesc.name=\"Description\"; desc.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\"; desc.resize(520,desc.height);\ncol.appendChild(desc);\n// spacing: use itemSpacing 24 and spacer? Different gaps: title→desc 20, desc→tools 24, tools→link 32. Use itemSpacing 24 uniformly, fine.\nconst tools=text(\"Sculpted in ZBrush, retopologized and UV-mapped in Maya, textured in Mari, rendered with Arnold.\",{size:14,style:\"Regular\",color:C.gray,lh:22});\ntools.name=\"Tools\"; tools.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\"; tools.resize(520,tools.height);\ncol.appendChild(tools);\nconst link=text(\"More shots from this project ↗\",{size:16,style:\"Medium\",color:C.accent}); link.name=\"Link\";\ncol.appendChild(link);\n// status pill\nconst pill=figma.createFrame(); pill.name=\"Status\"; pill.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\"; pill.itemSpacing=10;\npill.paddingLeft=14; pill.paddingRight=14; pill.paddingTop=8; pill.paddingBottom=8;\npill.cornerRadius=999; pill.strokes=solid(C.line)... \n```\npill: fill maybe #EDECE8, text gray \"Project WIP\". Add small dot rect? keep text only.\n```js\nconst pillText=text(\"Project WIP\",{size:13,style:\"Medium\",color:C.gray}); pill.appendChild(pillText);\npill.visible=false; col.appendChild(pill);\npb.appendChild(col);\n```\ncol.itemSpacing — with different children counts hidden still occupy? Hidden children in auto layout don't take space (visible=false removes from layout). \n\nBut wait: for tools color maybe slightly lighter gray. Fine same gray.\n\nRight side: instance of ImagePlaceholder:\n```js\nconst phComp = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(PH_ID); const phInst=phComp.createInstance(); \npb.appendChild(phInst);\n```\nphInst name